item.description:
Experts say the critical Senate race in Michigan could come down to Black voters in urban areas like Detroit. But is Democratic nominee Abdul El-Sayed taking this group for granted? Our team travels to Flint to hear from voters about what this outreach looks like.&nbsp;

---&nbsp;

Guest: Jeff Zeleny, CNN Chief National Affairs Correspondent&nbsp;

Host: David Rind&nbsp;

Producer: Paola Ortiz&nbsp;

Showrunner: Felicia Patinkin
Learn more about your ad choices. Visit podcastchoices.com/adchoices

